Z||000005||frontal lobe||10-18-2000||11:45 PM||||Definitely well written but also quite sick.<P>I would eat dog if I was starving, but I'm not and neither are most north americans.  There is NO WAY our culture is going to go for that.<P>It does bring up an interesting topic, though.  I've always found it interesting what meat is the dominant one in a culture.  The U.S. is primarily cow, chicken, and pig.  Not to be stupid, but not also to presume, is it the same in Canada?  On the other hand, I can hardly find lamb here in Wisconsin but the middle east and India cultures seem to prefer it to beef.<P>Whatever, the more pet-like the animal, the less likely I would be willing to eat it.  My west highland terrier is safe--18 pounds of dog that cost me $600 (yes, $600!) comes to over $35/lb even if he was all meat!||||reg||1
