Z||000008||ChadMan||10-19-2000||12:48 PM||||It's a joke, all right, and a good one too.  If you click "Products," then click "Gift Boxes," you get an elaborate and somewhat real-looking error-message except for the seventh line, which reads: "Server hates you."<P>It wouldn't surprise me if this site was created by some vegans who want us to think twice about eating meat of any kind.<P>As for me, I'm going to post some of my favorite recipes, including Poodles 'n' Noodles, Beagle Bisque, Kung Pao Collie, and Chow Chowder.<P>(Just kidding.  I think I'd kill and eat a middle manager before I'd kill and eat a dog.)||||reg||10
Z||000009||Black88GT||10-19-2000||02:42 PM||||ChadMan hit the nail on the head.  <P>I think this site was made by tree huggers oops I mean "vegetarians", because they always say things like "You wouldn't think of eating your dog but why is a hamburger any different" and all of that nonsense.<P>I think they just need to get a life and stop trying to tell me what to eat (I have a mother for that)<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000010||Patrick||10-19-2000||04:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>The U.S. is primarily cow, chicken, and pig. Not to be stupid, but not also to presume, is it the same in Canada?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>No, we tend to favor whale meat and moose in Canada. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Just kidding Frontal, our tastes are much the same as in the States.<P>Not too much beef is eaten in India where people of the Sikh religion regard cows as sacred. In the middle eastern countries, pork consumption is also limited because of religious beliefs. Orthodox Jews don't eat pork and I believe that some Arabs don't eat it either. They regard pigs as unclean and therefore unfit for eating. I suppose the eating of lamb helps to fill that protein void. The terrain and climate of a country also contributes to what animals can be successfully raised and used as a food source.||||reg||1
