Z||000013||Patrick||10-19-2000||08:05 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.kinzone.net/~PC000046/graphics/501.jpg">  <BR>This all reminds me of a movie my parents took me to see when I was eight years old back in 1963. The movie was called <B><I>Mondo Cane</I></B> (It's a Dog's World) and it both scared and fascinated me. Have a look at this link to read a short blurb about it. You'll understand why I remembered this movie after being involved in this thread.<P> <A HREF="http://www.kinzone.net/catalog/pulsetv/G200075:P200842/!SIDnz4TzBqwBb" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kinzone.net/catalog/pulsetv/G200075:P200842/!SIDnz4TzBqwBb</A> <P>It is a shocking but very well made documentary. If it's available for rent, I'd suggest checking it out if you have a strong disposition. This movie will definitely broaden your horizons.<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000014||Old Lar||10-19-2000||08:35 PM||||This is probably a joke,  But I got to spend some time in mainland China the past few years and anything that moves can be on the dinner plate.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/baskets.jpg"> <BR>So you have you basic fresh bird.  At the market you can get pidgeon, chicken, duck rabbit, snake, cat, dog.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cages.jpg"> <P>While there I got to eat snake..to many bones, frog.. rather slimy,..turtle.. eh, pidgeon was ok, eel too boney.. When I'd go through the cafeteria line. I'd ask my interpreter what the food was, the answer "meat",  I doubt that I had cat or dog, because it is rather expensive.  The food was butcherd fresh because of lack of refridgeration.<P>Fresh meat!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carcass.jpg"> <BR>You need to remember where the Chinese are coming from..some 30 million died from famine during the cultural revolution of the 60's.  Everything that moves is food.<P>No Fieros in China.<BR>||||reg||10
